{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1111111-0000-4000-a000-000000000001",
    "name": "Billing — Products",
    "description": "Billing product catalogue API (`/api/v1/product`).\n\n**Access model** — dooit authors the catalogue, clients read it:\n\n| | dooit | client |\n|---|---|---|\n| read (list, get, categories, meta) | yes | yes |\n| create / update / status / delete / bulk-import | yes | **403** |\n\nReads are open to clients on purpose: the catalogue names the rows on their\nusage table and invoices.\n\n## Setup\n1. Set `URL` (default `http://localhost:6830`).\n2. Run **Auth → Login (dooit)** — captures `{{token}}` automatically.\n3. Run **Auth → Login (client)** — captures `{{clientToken}}`, used by the\n   negative access-control tests.\n\nEvery request asserts its status code, so the whole collection can be run\nwith Newman as a smoke suite:\n\n```\nnewman run BillingProducts.postman_collection.json --env-var URL=http://localhost:6830\n```\n\nReference: docs/billingmodule/mongoose-schema.md",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "URL",
      "value": "http://localhost:6830",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "dooit JWT — set by Login (dooit)"
    },
    {
      "key": "clientToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "client JWT — set by Login (client)"
    },
    {
      "key": "dooitEmail",
      "value": "admin@dooit.ai",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "dooitPassword",
      "value": "CHANGE_ME",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "clientEmail",
      "value": "client@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "clientPassword",
      "value": "CHANGE_ME",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "productId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "set by Create Product"
    },
    {
      "key": "productCode",
      "value": "id_doc_verification",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Run these first — they capture the two JWTs the rest of the collection uses.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (dooit)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (res.token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', res.token);",
                  "  console.log('dooit token captured');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('token returned', () => pm.expect(res.token).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "",
                "disabled": true
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{dooitEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{dooitPassword}}\",\n  \"userType\": \"dooit\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{URL}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{URL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Captures {{token}}. userType must be sent (body or x-user-type header)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (client)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (res.token) pm.collectionVariables.set('clientToken', res.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "",
                "disabled": true
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{clientEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{clientPassword}}\",\n  \"userType\": \"client\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{URL}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{URL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Captures {{clientToken}} — used by the access-control tests."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
